<title>GERMANY: Siemens unit sees stable 96/97 sales, profit.</title>
<headline>Siemens unit sees stable 96/97 sales, profit.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified manufacturer Siemens AG said on Monday its automation unit expected stable sales and profit in 1996/97 without factoring in results from its recent acquisition of AEG Electrocom.</p>
<p>Siemens Automation (AUT) also said it expected noticeable improvement in 1997/98 and aimed to expand sales to 10 billion marks ($6.1 billion) and raise its return to seven percent in 10 years. The unit had 6.6 billion marks in sales and 509 million marks in pretax profit in the year that ended September 30.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150 ($ = 1.642 German Marks)</p>
</text>
